From: mscharged-port
Subject: Run European revision 1 data on the revision 2 code
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Owner decision: a European revision 1 disc plays with the game code of
revision 2. Three data contracts changed between the revisions (checked on
both discs): revision 2 inserted FE_GEN_Music at 0x1A of the sound bank table
in audio/nlxgs.bun, so every later bank sits one higher; it inserted
presentation script native 63 (PRESENTATION_SET_STADIUM_EFFECTS_ENABLED), so
the natives after it are numbered one higher; and it gave the in-game texture
pool less room (revision 1 0x966666, revision 2 0x900000) for its smaller
stadiums. For a revision 1 disc the host turns these adapters on whatever the
tweak set: LoadSoundBank maps the bank to revision 1's table (FE_GEN_Music to
STREAM_GEN_Music, which revision 1 loads in the same step), DoFunctionCall
renumbers revision 1's natives from 63, and the pool gets revision 1's budget.
Every other script, menu and text file is the same on both discs.

diff --git a/src/Game/AsyncLoading.cpp b/src/Game/AsyncLoading.cpp
index d1bfd4d..e639924 100644
--- a/src/Game/AsyncLoading.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/AsyncLoading.cpp
@@ -1979,6 +1979,11 @@ void InitializeGameState1(AsyncLoadingManager* manager)
     requirements[1].mSize = 0x900000;
 #else
     requirements[1].mSize = 0x8B3333;
+#endif
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // European revision 1 data: its larger stadiums need revision 1's
+    // texture budget (tweak patch 0019).
+    requirements[1].mSize = mscharged_tweak_rev1_ingame_texture_budget(requirements[1].mSize);
 #endif
     requirements[2].mSize = 0x580000;
     glSetCurrentResourcePool(glCreateResourcePool(requirements, 3, "InGame"));
